    "decision": "db_pool_size = 10, db_max_overflow = 10",
    "interpretation": "20/20 beat 5/10 on throughput in 3/3 paired rounds (+4.3% median), with p95 flat; small, and 3/3 can happen by chance 1 time in 8. 10/10 matched 20/20 on throughput (+0.1%) and p95 (-0.6%); 20/20 had a lower p50 (-5.2%). A likely cause: with pool_size 5, connections above 5 are closed on return and reopened under load. 10/10 caps a process at 20 connections, so two app instances plus one finalizer use at most 60 of Postgres's default 100; 20/20 would allow 120."
